# Replace @your-github-username below with the people who should review any
# change that could reach the API key (one or more usernames or @org/team names).
#
# Anything the deploy workflow executes can read GOOGLE_TRANSLATE_API_KEY,
# which is billed to a real account. Changes to these paths need review from
# someone who knows what that means.
#
# /.github/ covers this file too: without that, a pull request could remove
# these rules with an approval from anyone.
#
# Book content is deliberately not owned. Pages and pinned translations cannot
# reach the key, and gating them would make the owners a bottleneck on the
# actual writing.
#
# These rules only block merges once "Require review from Code Owners" is on
# for the main branch (see the kit's README).

/.github/    @your-github-username
/scripts/    @your-github-username
